  "headline": "Criterion (iii) as posed is 0.0 at N=8 -- but that zero is an EMPTY INTERSECTION, not an absent capability. No candidate (0 of 40) is simultaneously dynamics-clean by (i) and goal-satisfiable by (ii). Dropping the conjunction, 2 of 40 candidates reach a satisfiable goal AND a found plan, and best-of-N finds them: unconditional (iii) yield goes 0.0 at N=1 to 0.4 at N=8, and the SHIPPED pipeline's own conjunction (trust gate AND goal AND plan) goes 0.0 to 0.2. Selecting on dynamics accuracy is not merely insufficient for plannability -- on this grid it is anti-selective: on tn36 the six candidates with held-out accuracy 1.0 (17 of 17 changing transitions exact) ALL fail the goal gate, while the one candidate whose goal is satisfiable and plannable scores 0.235.",
